text:
Mia Wang: Quick check - compact left nav + deep links: keep a tiny breadcrumb or rely on the header? noticed workspace filter drops with short links :thinking_face:
Jamie Lee: I'd keep a slim breadcrumb for landing context. If we hide it, header must always expose workspace and be focusable for keyboard users.
Omar Khan: Routing contract: canonical path `/w/:ws/...`. Accept `/models/:id?ws=` but rewrite to canonical on first paint so hydration and analytics stay consistent.
Nora Patel: A11y nits: crumbs must sit in a `nav` landmark, active crumb gets `aria-current=\"page\"`, truncated text needs `aria-label`. For mobile, long-press should open an accessible sheet (role=dialog) with actions.
Mia Wang: UX: condensed breadcrumb = single line, smaller type, ellipsize workspace. On very small widths hide workspace and reveal via sheet. Tooltips ok desktop only.
nav-bot: Spec draft published: https://redwood.design/ux/compact-crumbs - includes canary plan and a11y checklist.
Jamie Lee: Hydration snippet (tiny):
```
// run once
const u = new URL(window.location.href);
if (u.searchParams.has('ws') && u.pathname.startsWith('/models/')) {
  const ws = u.searchParams.get('ws');
  const id = u.pathname.split('/').pop();
  history.replaceState({}, '', `/w/${ws}/models/${id}` + u.search);
  telemetry.track('rewrite_query_ws_to_path');
}
// migrate old hashes to query
if (window.location.hash.includes('panel=')) {
  const h = new URLSearchParams(window.location.hash.slice(1));
  const p = h.get('panel');
  if (p) { u.searchParams.set('panel', p); history.replaceState({}, '', u.pathname + '?' + u.searchParams.toString()); telemetry.track('migrate_hash_panel'); }
}
```
Omar Khan: Also add `?preserveNav=0|1` for embeds; default to 1. Router should avoid encoding UI-only state in path segments.
Nora Patel: Microcopy: mobile sheet action = "Open parent workspace"; breadcrumb toggle label = "Show path" for screen readers. Ensure focus outline contrast >= 4.5:1.
Mia Wang: I'll update mocks and post frames tomorrow. Thanks all :sparkles:
